WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
RETO MEIER: Today I learned that
every 311 complaint, police,

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.520
and fire department incident,
bike share ride, street tree,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.620
and filming location
in San Francisco

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.980
is now available in a
BigQuery public data set.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.900
I'm Reto Meier, Google
Developer advocate.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.630
Join me as I explore the city
by the bay with BigQuery.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.680
SF, Fog City, whatever
you want to call it,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.590
it's just a short
traffic-congested drive

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.900
up the 101 from here
in Mountain View.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.200
So grab your jacket, and let's
head for the golden city.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.270
Really?

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.920
Come on.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.220
In 2016, there were almost
a half million 311 calls

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.340
in San Francisco, compared to
over 2 million in New York.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.250
So clearly, there's a lot
less to complain about out

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.140
here on the bes--

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:49.920
what?

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.848
Per capita?

00:00:50.848 --> 00:00:53.190
Oh.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.010
San Francisco, home to
over 800,000 people,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.130
is a city that makes good
use of its 311 service using

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.500
the municipal complaints
line, 2 and 1/2 times more

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.580
often per capita
than New Yorkers.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.450
The most common complaints
in San Francisco

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.140
are for graffiti, and requests
for street or sidewalk

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.910
cleaning, while
bulky item pickups

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.560
and illegal homeless
encampments are

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.200
the fastest growing complaints.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.900
San Franciscans are getting
less easily offended,

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.610
with inoffensive
graffiti complaints

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:23.220
on the up, while there's
been a significant drop

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.320
in offensive graffiti.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.860
The SFPD data includes more
than two million incidents

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.190
since 2003.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.150
So we know that as we
head down Bryant Street,

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.720
we should keep an eye out.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.830
Theft from locked cars
accounts for over 17%

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.810
of all reported crime
incidents in San Francisco.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.640
And Bryant Street is a notable
hotspot, peaking on Fridays,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.240
with most reports filed at
lunchtime or after work.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.730
This heat map shows
the worst places

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.770
to park if you're
planning to leave anything

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.870
valuable in your car
and want it to still

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.090
be there when you get back.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.180
It turns out a lot of stuff
goes missing here on Bryant.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.660
Nearly 20% of filed
lost property reports

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.065
are from Bryant Street.

00:02:04.065 --> 00:02:06.600
The best odds for
finding something

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.150
is here, over on,
Valencia, where

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.650
more than twice
as many items are

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.750
found than are reported lost.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.810
Meanwhile, on Haight, the
legalization of cannabis

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.880
could see a 7%
reduction in the number

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.680
of arrests in the
Haight-Ashbury neighborhood.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.870
In 2016, 26% of all drug-related
arrests in San Francisco

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.130
were for marijuana.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.570
But as you can see, drug
arrests are down 62% since 2003,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.270
with only methamphetamine
arrests trending up.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:37.140
2016 marked the first time meth
became the most common involved

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.030
in an arrest here in the city.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:42.705
With access to details for more
than 120,000 sidewalk trees,

00:02:42.705 --> 00:02:44.580
we know that you can
get a taste for Monterey

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:48.270
by visiting Sunset Boulevard,
the leafiest street in San

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.560
Francisco.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.760
Home to nearly 1,400 Monterey
pines and Monterey cypress, SF

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.560
is a shadier city than
New York, featuring

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.910
2,600 trees per square mile,
compared to New York's 2,200.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:02.370
But they share the London
plane as the most common tree

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.960
in both cities.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.260
For cyclists, this
trail along Embarcadero

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.330
is the most common path
for Bay Area Bike Share

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.550
riders in San Francisco.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.010
After looking at nearly
a million trip records,

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.890
we learned that San
Francisco bike sharers

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.540
spend an average of
14 minutes per trip,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.680
almost the same as the 15-minute
average for New Yorkers.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.480
We'll blame the steep hills for
the slower average trip speeds

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.520
here on the west coast.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.010
The 4 million fire department
service calls show us that

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.220
the most common location
for a structural fire is

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:35.550
in the Tenderloin, while the
best place for it to happen,

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.040
if its' going to
happen, is in Chinatown,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.920
where the average response
between calling 911 and firemen

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.910
arriving at your burning
building is an impressive four

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.830
minutes, 30 seconds, compared
to a city wide average of six

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.720
minutes and eight seconds.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.490
Big shout out to
the crew of Engine 3

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:53.010
of the 4th battalion, the
fastest engine in the west,

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.730
with an average response time
of just over three minutes.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:59.520
Thanks to the city and county
of San Francisco's OpenData

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.610
project, and Bay Area Bike
Share, Google BigQuery's

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.460
public data sets now
include over 150 gigabytes

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.700
of San Francisco public
data for you to explore.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.030
As always, your first terabyte
of processing is free.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.974
So fire up BigQuery today to
investigate San Francisco.

00:04:13.974 --> 00:04:15.890
And share you results
with us, using the Today

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.880
I Learned With
Big Query hashtag.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.800
And as always, subscribe
to our channel,

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.450
and follow our blog to learn
something new with BigQuery.

